{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '170,310p' collab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md; cat collab/1792083677000-architect-frame-nan-review.report.md; cat collab/1793400000000-architect-phase8-closing.report.md\"","aggregated_output":"| 3 | G9 Dart slow-tier run and attribution | lane time only | read before any code |\n| 4 | G12 P2 pair: `decode*` key equality + binder-refusal defence | 1 day, 2 rounds | rows_test, debruijn kernel tests |\n| 5 | G12 P3 test slice: 8d successor tests, delete `malformed-vectors`, `parity_test` `:refer` tidy | 0.5 day | quick tier |\n| 6 | §5 doc pass + G10/G13 wording + UCF clause 10 record | 0.5 day, 1 round | Architect read |\n| 7 | owner rulings on G3/G4 (then 0.5-1 day each), G6, G7 (6d) | as §1.2 | after rulings only |\n\n**Verdict: the design is complete except X1-X4 of §0.** `yin.vm.semantic` as the frozen design specifies it is finished and verified in the tree; the remaining work is one P1 on the carrier's link pendings, one half-day refusal that closes a silent-hang hazard in the backends, one missing Dart slow-tier run, and owner-gated capability questions that the design deliberately left outside the kernel.\n\nGAP-LIST-READY\nCreated-GMT: 2026-10-15 16:57:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-15 23:57:00 +07\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-15 17:01:17 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-16 00:01:17 +07\nCoding-Agent: claude (claude-fable-5-1)\nSession-ID: pending\nBrief: ./collab/1793320000000-architect-frame-nan-review.prompt.md\nEngineer report: ./collab/1792082835156-engineer-frame-nan.report.md\nBranch: srvm-frame-nan @ 6dceede9 (uncommitted, 5 files +71/-5); read-only review, one throwaway probe test ns created and deleted, tree unchanged\n\n# Architect review: frame.cljc / rows.cljc NaN follow-up\n\n## 1. Verdict\n\nThe change is the fix shape my 8f-3 ruling §5 prescribed, at the right site,\nwith the right guards, and the second site codex found in `rows.cljc` is a\nreal instance of the same class. The tests are genuine on the hosts that\nmatter. One pre-existing sibling rule (host `distinct` on literal keys in\n`decode*`) is deliberately left alone by codex and I agree it is a different\nrule, but it is host-divergent and belongs in the ledger (P2 below, not\nblocking). Sign-off at the end, conditional only on green Node and Dart\nlanes, which the brief assigns to the orchestrator.\n\n## 2. Judgements, in the brief's order\n\n### (1) `frame.cljc` `bindings=`\n\nCorrect.\n\n- NaN: `cbor/content=` keys every NaN to `[::float64 :nan]`, so fresh and\n  literal NaN compare equal; nested NaN recurses through `content-key`.\n- Signed zero: `[::float64 neg e f]` keeps 0.0 apart from -0.0. The test\n  pins that a 0.0 binding against a -0.0 free-env is `:free-env-mismatch`.\n  This IS a behaviour change from host `=` (which merged them) and it is the\n  right one: both sides of this comparison are decoded canonical data (see\n  below), so a sign difference is a genuine content difference.\n- Guards: `fn?`/`values/closure?`/`values/continuation?` and the\n  `:stream-ref`/`:cursor-ref`/`:cell-ref` `:type` map are exactly\n  `data/callable?` and `data/ref?` (data.cljc 453-463); the\n  `identical?` → guard → `content=` ordering is `data-content=` verbatim.\n  `Closure` and `Continuation` are `deftype`s (values.cljc 39, 75), not\n  records, so `content-key`'s `map?` branch never walks them even when they\n  sit inside a collection (`:else x` → host `=`).\n- Key-set comparison: `(= (set (keys a)) (set (keys b)))` over symbols is\n  host-neutral; a nil-valued binding versus an absent key is caught here,\n  not by `get`.\n- Non-NaN behaviour changes, exhaustively: (a) 0.0 vs -0.0 now refuse on all\n  hosts; (b) on Dart, an int vs a float of one value (1 vs 1.0) now refuse\n  where cljd `=` accepted (the JVM already refused, so this aligns Dart with\n  the JVM); (c) decimals of one value and different scale now refuse (host\n  `=` merged them). All three are canonical-bytes differences. No value that\n  was unequal before becomes equal: lists/vectors were already merged by\n  host `=`, metadata was already ignored, and records do not occur because\n  in the only caller (`rows.cljc` `validate-frames`, 1109-1144) BOTH the\n  frame bindings and `:free-env` come through `decoded-value` from the wire,\n  so neither side ever holds a host object, a record, or an unencodable\n  number. That also disposes of the one risk in `content-key` (it can\n  `refuse` on an unportable number): nothing unportable reaches it here.\n\n### (2) `rows.cljc` `decode*` row-order check\n\nSame bug, correctly fixed, no site missed within the NaN class.\n\n- Old check: `(= (vec slots) (ordered-slots kind (vec slots)))`, whole\n  vector, host `=`. `ordered-slots` (161-169) re-sorts the very same slot\n  objects, so on the JVM identity saves it; on JS the number `-equiv` and on\n  Dart IEEE `==` make any row carrying a NaN literal (`[:lit NaN]` in a\n  `:bindings`, `:map`, `:store`, `:set`, ... row) `:row-order` regardless of\n  order. That is exactly the 8f-3 class.\n- New check is slotwise `content=`. `ordered-slots` preserves length by\n  construction (a permutation of `slots`, or `slots` itself for the `:else`\n  kinds), so `map` truncates nothing; for the `:else` kinds every slot is\n  `identical?` and `content=` short-circuits without a traversal.\n- Equivalence for non-NaN input: both checks accept every row whose slots\n  are already in canonical order. They differ only where host `=` merged\n  byte-distinct literals in a mis-ordered row (0.0/-0.0, decimal scale,\n  Dart int/float), where the old check wrongly accepted a non-canonical\n  order; the new check refuses, and that refusal is host-neutral. No\n  previously refused row is now accepted: `content=` is stricter than host\n  `=` everywhere except NaN. Codex's \"no callable/ref guard needed\" is right:\n  wire slots are `[:lit x]`, `[:row id]`, `[:cursor-cell n]`, keywords and\n  integers, all encodable.\n- Other sites (I re-read codex's survey against the code): the byte\n  comparison at 113-115, the address/hash checks (912-921), `check-literal-\n  markers!`, and the reachability/count checks are not value comparisons.\n  `rows/checkpoint.cljc` 77 is a kind keyword. Agreed.\n- The sibling I want recorded (P2, not this slice): `decode*` 931-935\n  `:duplicate-key` has two clauses; the second is byte-level and\n  host-neutral, the first is host `distinct` over the literal keys. JVM\n  probe (throwaway ns, deleted): `(count (distinct [0.0 -0.0]))` = 1, and a\n  `:map` or `:set` row with keys `0.0` and `-0.0` is **emitted** by\n  `rows/emit` and then **refused** by `rows/decode` as `:duplicate-key`,\n  path = the row id. On Dart cljd `=` also merges 1 and 1.0, so a\n  JVM-emitted `#{1 1.0}` would decode on the JVM and refuse on Dart. This is\n  host equality on literal slots, but it is a different rule (host\n  representability of the decoded map/set, same intent as line 811), not\n  the reflexivity bug, and it is not NaN-divergent: two NaN keys are\n  refused by the byte clause on every host. Codex classified it the same way\n  and left it; correct call for this slice. It needs a ledger row:\n  \"emit/decode asymmetry and Dart-only refusal for byte-distinct,\n  host-equal literal keys (0.0/-0.0 everywhere, 1/1.0 on Dart)\". Fix shape\n  when taken: decide whether the rule belongs at the wire (then drop the\n  host clause and keep bytes) or at the decoded host value (then `emit`\n  must refuse what `decode` refuses).\n\n### (3) Tests are real\n\n- `free-env-compares-values-by-content`: 30 assertions across the three\n  contexts. On the JVM the fresh-box `(* 1.0 ##NaN)` versus `##NaN` is a\n  genuine non-identical pair, so the JVM lane tests the NaN path too (the\n  mutant log confirms: 9 failures = 3 contexts × {fresh NaN, nested NaN,\n  signed zero}). On JS/Dart the same assertions fail before the fix for the\n  identical-NaN reason. The `(is (not (cbor/content= 0.0 -0.0)))` line is a\n  library fact rather than a frame fact; harmless, keep.\n- `nan-valued-row-slots-are-canonical`: yes, it still tests the NaN path.\n  The cursor references were added only to satisfy the reference-free\n  collection-row rule; they do not shield the NaN slot. On JS/Dart the old\n  whole-vector `=` fails on the `[:lit NaN]` slot even when no reordering\n  happens, so each of the three decodes would have been `:row-order` there.\n  On the JVM this test cannot fail before or after (identity), which is why\n  it is a lane test; it is correctly written as portable `.cljc`.\n- I re-ran `frame-test` + `rows-test` on the JVM: 49 tests / 939 assertions,\n  0 failures, 0 errors (codex's 116/1380 included `vm-test` and\n  `effects-test`; consistent).\n\n### (4) Known-gaps row\n\nAccurate as of this review. Two wording nits for the orchestrator at\nlanding (P3): replace \"closed in uncommitted frame-nan follow-up\" with the\ncommit hash, and the row still says `frame.cljc:141`; the comparison now\nsits at 159 (the old line number remains a fair historical pointer, so\neither leave it or write \"formerly :141\"). Add the P2 sibling row from (2).\n\n### (5) Scope\n\nClean: exactly `frame.cljc`, `rows.cljc`, the two matching tests and the\nledger row. No `docs/design`, no `src/yang`, no `test/yang`. Both new\nrequires (`cbor`, `values`) are used. `git status` after my probe deletion\nshows only the five tracked edits plus collab files.\n\n## 3. P1 / P2 / P3\n\n- P1: none.\n- P2-1 (ledger, not this slice): `decode*` 931-935 host-`distinct` clause,\n  emit/decode asymmetry for 0.0/-0.0 keys on every host and a Dart-only\n  refusal for 1/1.0 keys. Record in `docs/agents/known-gaps.md`, owner\n  yin.vm.semantic, open.\n- P3-1: ledger row wording at landing (commit hash, line pointer).\n- P3-2: `frame_test` line 242 asserts a `cbor` library fact inside a frame\n  test; cosmetic.\n\n## 4. What the Node and Dart lanes must show (orchestrator runs after sign)\n\n`bb test:cljs` then `bb test:cljd` (foreground, one lane at a time, per\n`docs/agents/build-n-test.md`). Expect, per lane:\n\n- \"Testing yin.vm.semantic.frame-test\" and \"Testing yin.vm.ucf.rows-test\"\n  both present in the output (discovery proof).\n- 0 failures, 0 errors overall. Before this change both lanes would have\n  reported 6 failures in `free-env-compares-values-by-content` (fresh NaN\n  and nested NaN acceptance in each of three contexts) and 3 failures in\n  `nan-valued-row-slots-are-canonical` (each decode refusing `:row-order`);\n  their absence is the evidence.\n- Assertion counts for the two namespaces equal to the JVM's minus any\n  documented JVM-only skips; `frame-test` should add exactly 30 and\n  `rows-test` exactly 6 relative to the previous lane run.\n- Dart: a `(* 1.0 ##NaN)` is a plain Dart NaN; if `(not= value value)`\n  style checks appear anywhere in the lane they are unaffected by this\n  change.\n\nIf either lane shows a failure in either new deftest, do not patch forward:\nrevert the slice and reopen (Q6 standing rule).\n\nSIGN-OFF\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-16 11:45:00 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-16 18:45:00 +07\nCoding-Agent: claude (claude-fable-5-1), Architect\nSession-ID: pending\n\n# Architect closing sign-off: srvm-phase8 at c11f9299 (delta since the final review at 6dceede9)\n\nBrief: ./collab/1793390000000-architect-phase8-closing.prompt.md\nWorktree: datomworld-srvm-p8final = origin/srvm-phase8 @ c11f9299. Read-only; the only file written is this report. `git status` shows no tracked change.\n\n## Delta\n\n`git log --oneline 6dceede9..HEAD`: 8 commits, 3 first-parent merges, each with one slice commit beneath except the frame-NaN merge (two):\n\n| merge | parents | slice commits |\n|---|---|---|\n| 65e1ec81 ledger docs | 6dceede9 + 4d727e0c | 4d727e0c (docs only) |\n| 47249651 frame-NaN | 65e1ec81 + 51c1294a | 4accc7e9 (signed off), 51c1294a (cljs guard) |\n| c11f9299 Node slow-C4 floats | 47249651 + 6af0ddd2 | 0ca2c0f9 (fixture + pin), 6af0ddd2 (pin replacement text) |\n\n`git diff --stat 6dceede9..HEAD`: 8 files, +113/-13, and nothing else:\n\n- `docs/agents/known-gaps.md` (+5/-2)\n- `docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md` (+8)\n- `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/frame.cljc` (+21/-3)\n- `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc` (+3/-1)\n- `test/yang/python/antlr/prelude_parity_test.cljc` (+4/-7)\n- `test/yin/vm/semantic/frame_test.cljc` (+35)\n- `test/yin/vm/semantic/load_paths_test.cljc` (+23)\n- `test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc` (+14)\n\nNo `src/yang/**`, no fixture under `test/resources`, no collab or secret path. The only C4 file touched is `prelude_parity_test.cljc`, which is the one my Node slow-C4 ruling named under the 8f freeze rule.\n\n## Piece by piece\n\n### 1. Ledger-docs merge 65e1ec81 (my P2-1 / P2-2 / P3 rows)\n\n**verified** against the final report §6:\n\n- P2-1: `yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md` I-6 gains one dated paragraph (lines 647-654) saying `rows-checkpoint-v3.txt` re-minted at 8c because the installs child moved `\"v3\"` → `\"v4\"`, three child addresses moved, no format/profile/H/R/descriptor in any pack. That is my §4 item 1 wording. Met.\n- P2-2: the native-binder-refusal row now reads \"accepted as design for the phase 8 merge (the projection is the only producer … §3.4, defence in depth, not a hole); follow-up slice to be scheduled by the owner\". That is the second of the two options I offered. Met.\n- P3-2: the 8d partial-mappings row is added (\"open: name two successor tests\"). Met.\n- P3-4: the \"22 of 22\" row records namespaces run by `~/ci/slow-tier.sh`, not deftests, 231 `^:slow` in tree. Met; the Node slow line it promises is now on file (piece 3).\n- P3-1 (prose pass over seven docs) and P3-3 (`:refer` tidy, `malformed-vectors` deletion) were allowed to follow the merge and are not in the delta. Still open, still P3.\n\nDocs only; no code in this merge. Matches.\n\n### 2. Frame-NaN merge 47249651\n\n**verified** that 4accc7e9 is exactly the signed-off shape: `frame.cljc` adds `bindings=` (slotwise `cbor/content=` with host `=` retained for fns, closures, continuations and `:stream-ref`/`:cursor-ref`/`:cell-ref` maps, the same opacity set `data-content=` uses) and the free-env check at the former `:141` now calls it; `rows.cljc` `decode*` compares decoded row order slotwise by `cbor/content=` instead of host `=`; `frame_test` adds `free-env-compares-values-by-content` over `:wait`/`:captured`/`:parked`; `rows_test` adds `nan-valued-row-slots-are-canonical` (bindings, set, map; emit → decode → emit root stable). The ledger row for `frame.cljc` is closed on the branch with the evidence link, and the new P2 row for the `decode*` host-`distinct` clause on map/set keys (0.0/-0.0 asymmetry, Dart-only 1/1.0 refusal) is the P2-1 of that review. The review report itself (`*architect-frame-nan-review.report.md`) is not in this worktree's `collab/` and the main checkout is outside this session's allowed directories, so the match is to the merge subject, the ledger row text and the code I signed; the code is unchanged from 4accc7e9 at HEAD (`git show 4accc7e9` diff of the three non-test files is byte-identical to the HEAD delta).\n\n**verified** 51c1294a is the one later commit and does only what the brief says: the two signed-zero assertions (`0.0` vs `-0.0` free binding → `:free-env-mismatch`; `(not (cbor/content= 0.0 -0.0))`) are wrapped in `#?@(:cljs [] :default [...])` with a comment. Correct: JS has one zero, so the carrier cannot distinguish them there and the assertion would be a false red on Node, not a kernel divergence. No other line changed (+7/-4 in `frame_test.cljc`).\n\n**Merged known-gaps.md**: 0 conflict markers in `known-gaps.md` and `ucf-revisions.md`; 25 table rows, 0 duplicate lines; exactly one row mentions `frame.cljc` (the closed one; the old open row is gone), exactly one native-binder row (the amended one). Row count reconciles: 22 at 6dceede9, +3 net from the ledger merge (binder amended in place, 8d, 22/22) = 25 at 65e1ec81 (my earlier number of 24 was wrong by the binder row being modified, not added), frame-NaN amended the frame row in place and added the `decode*` row; the conflict resolution kept both the ledger rows and the frame-NaN rows, which is the right union. No damage.\n\n### 3. Node slow-C4 fix merge c11f9299\n\n**verified** 0ca2c0f9 applies F1 of my ruling verbatim: the three `py/float-mod` rows become `(py/mod {:py/float …} {:py/float …})` with `{:py/float …}` expectations, and the reducer loses the `py/float-mod` special case so every row is `(ops/exact-literals (with-float64 f))`. No `src/` change, `int_ops_test` untouched (the optional docstring trim was not taken; fine).\n\n**verified** the pin at HEAD in `load_paths_test.cljc` is the F2 shape with the replacement text the brief says I prescribed in the node-pin diagnosis (that report is also outside this worktree): the portable half is unchanged from F2 (float64 `1.0E20` through both lanes, `(= rows datoms)`, address `blake3-d034b2a4…46b6`); the cljs half now keeps `linearize/project` and `project-datoms` inside the `thrown-with-msg?` form and asserts both lanes refuse with \"unsafe integral JavaScript number\". That is what 6af0ddd2's subject says (\"keeps projection inside the assertion; the row lane refuses at projection on JS\") and it is the correct tightening of my F2, whose cljs half assumed projection accepts the bare Number and only load refuses; the Node run showed the row lane refuses earlier, and the pin now covers both lanes regardless of which stage refuses. The address assertion held on the JVM here (below), so no re-pin was needed.\n\n**Gate evidence**:\n\n| lane | source | status |\n|---|---|---|\n| JVM, `frame-test` + `load-paths-test` + `rows-test` at c11f9299 | rerun here | **verified**: 52 tests, 1076 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors; counterexample searches 0 failures |\n| JVM, `prelude-parity-test` (`^:slow`) | not runnable here (`DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1` needs an approval this session does not have) | **reported** green by the 0ca2c0f9 step 4 (my ruling's JVM probe of the three rows also passed before the edit) |\n| Node slow (jupiter) after the fix | brief | **reported**: 55 tests, 658 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n| Node slow-C4 full run before the fix | brief + `collab/node-slow-c4-prelude-failure.txt` | **reported**: 257 tests, 69 failures = 66 `dht-import-test` + 3 prelude rows; the failure text on file is exactly the cbor refusal my ruling diagnosed, with the `:ast-walker` side passing |\n| Dart pin | brief / merge subject | **reported**: +38 green |\n\nThe Node and Dart numbers are the orchestrator's; I could not build either lane here (no `node_modules`, no `lib/cljd-out`). The 55/658 line is for the lane the fix was aimed at and leaves `dht-import-test` as the only red in the full run (69 − 3 = 66, all `dht-import-test`).\n\n## Conditions of the final review\n\n| condition | owner | status |\n|---|---|---|\n| (a) jupiter Node slow-C4 line on file with `dht-import-test` the only red | orchestrator | **met**: full run 257/69 with 66 = `dht-import-test` and the other 3 fixed by c11f9299; post-fix prelude lane 55/658/0 |\n| (b) owner ruling on who regenerates `dht-import-v1.edn` and in which commit | **owner** | **not in the delta, not required to be**: `test/resources/yang/python/dht-import-v1.edn` is still untouched on this branch; the ledger carries the red. This remains the owner's call and does not block the merge |\n| P2-1 doc line | orchestrator | met (65e1ec81) |\n| P2-2 row | orchestrator + owner (slice to schedule) | met as \"accepted as design\"; the follow-up slice is the owner's to schedule |\n| §7 item 4, lift the C4 freeze and name the moved `test/yang` files | **owner** | post-merge; now 13 files (the 12 plus `prelude_parity_test.cljc` again), the yang.python seat must be told |\n| §7 item 5 follow-ups | owner | `frame.cljc` NaN: **closed** on this branch; binder-refusal defence, §2 prose pass, `malformed-vectors` deletion: open P2/P3, post-merge |\n\n## Findings\n\n| id | sev | where | finding | ask |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| P3-1 | P3 | `docs/agents/known-gaps.md`, `decode*` row | new P2 from the frame-NaN review (host-`distinct` on 0.0/-0.0 and 1/1.0 keys) has no slice assigned | assign with the binder-refusal slice; not a merge blocker, it is a pre-existing asymmetry the content-equality change made visible |\n| P3-2 | P3 | `test/yang/python/antlr/int_ops_test.cljc` `exact-literals` docstring | \"callers skip the float-only rows\" is now stale (no caller skips) | one-line trim in a later C4 edit, the yang.python seat's file |\n| P3-3 | P3 | record | the frame-NaN review report and the node-pin diagnosis are not in this worktree's `collab/`; this closing review matched code to the merge subjects, the ledger text and my own rulings | copy them into this worktree's `collab/` (cp -n) before the worktree is removed, per the standing collab rule |\n\nNo P1, no P2. Nothing in the delta is outside what I approved or prescribed; the two post-sign-off commits (51c1294a, 6af0ddd2) are test-only host guards whose reasoning I confirmed.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**SIGN-OFF at c11f9299.** The delta is the three merges the brief lists and nothing else; each matches the approved or prescribed shape; the merged ledger has no marker or duplicate damage and carries the right union of rows; condition (a) of the final review is met by the Node slow line on file, and condition (b) remains the owner's ruling on `dht-import-v1.edn`, which the ledger already carries and which does not gate the merge. Merge `srvm-phase8` to master at c11f9299.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
