carries. It replaces yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint at the\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Format records (section 5)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def stack-format\n  \"The `:yin.debruijn.code` format record: stack images identified by H\n   under the \\\"b2\\\" contract (`vm/stack-contract`), one canonical vector\n   per image. Free names are `:load-free` operands, definitions\n   `:store-put` and `:define` operands, application sites the call\n   opcodes -- all position-bearing by pc (section 5.3).\"\n  {:format              :yin.debruijn.code,\n   :contract            vm/stack-contract,\n   :identity-fn         debruijn-code/image-hash,\n   :identity-matches-fn (fn [H v] (= H (debruijn-code/image-hash v))),\n   :row-defect-fn       debruijn-code/image-defect,\n   :validate-fn         debruijn-code/image-defect,\n   :obligations-fn      stack-free-occurrences,\n   :definitions-fn      vector-definition-occurrences,\n   :applications-fn     vector-application-sites,\n   :parts-fn            (constantly nil)})\n\n\n(def register-format\n  \"The `:yin.debruijn.register` format record: register images identified\n   by R under the \\\"r2\\\" contract (`vm/register-contract`), one image\n   map per image. Free names are `[:load-free rd name]` operands across\n   all bodies, definitions the `:store-put` and `:define` keys,\n   application sites the call opcodes (section 5.4).\"\n  {:format              :yin.debruijn.register,\n   :contract            vm/register-contract,\n(ns yin.vm.semantic.layout\n  \"Phase 6c (docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md §4):\n   the de Bruijn register and stack kernels reconstruct the canonical\n   frame of the semantic kernel through their layouts, and lower it\n   back.\n\n   Static half, per segment A: `segment` derives R(A) and H(A) and reads\n   off the register pairing (`phys`, the restricted inverse `virt`, the\n   kernel's `live` as live-out with tail boundaries `[]`), the stack\n   correspondence (`h->a`, `a->h`, every `:push` removed) and the operand\n   layout `stack-layout` (the values pushed and not yet consumed while\n   control is inside a pc's expression). A `space` indexes segments by\n   the kernels' image identities, R and H, which are checksums: A is the\n   only code identity.\n\n   Dynamic half: `lift-state` reads a kernel's wait entry, parked record\n   or reified payload as the canonical `act` or `tail` payload the\n   semantic evaluator mints (`{:segment A :pc :env :window :k\n   :deliver}`, `{:segment A :site :k :deliver}`, engine fields carried);\n   `lower-state` is its inverse. The semantic kernel's return\n   destinations are recovered from A, never from the physical `:dest`;\n   the stack kernel's operand stack is sliced `[previous-base, base)` per\n(ns yin.vm.semantic.scan\n  \"Dependency facts derived from admitted semantic register vectors.\"\n  (:require [dao.space.query :as query]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn :as debruijn]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.ucf :as ucf]))\n\n\n(defn- bodies\n  [v]\n  (when-let [defect (code/well-formed? v)]\n    (throw (ex-info \"Cannot scan malformed semantic register vector\" defect)))\n  (code/parse v))\n\n\n(defn- chain\n  [v bs i]\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Semantic bytecode: flat content-addressed rows\n;; =============================================================================\n;; docs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md §2. One row `[id tag & slots]` per\n;; distinct node; `id` is `(jing/segment-key [tag & slots])`.\n\n(def semantic-bytecode-grammar\n  \"The §2.3 tag table: tag -> ordered `[field kind]` slots. Position `i` of a\n   row body (after the tag) holds the map field named at `i`, so this one\n   table drives both projection and reconstruction.\"\n  {:literal [[:value :data]],\n   :variable [[:name :sym]],\n   :lambda [[:params :syms] [:body :node]],\n   :application [[:operator :node] [:operands :nodes] [:tail? :bool]],\n   :if [[:test :node] [:consequent :node] [:alternate :node]],\n   :dao.stream.apply/call [[:op :kw] [:operands :nodes]],\n   :vm/gensym [[:prefix :str]],\n   :vm/store-get [[:key :key]],\n   :vm/store-put [[:key :key] [:val :data]],\n   :vm/current-continuation [],\n   :vm/park [],\nrg: docs/design/yin.vm.ucf.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:5:completion audit. Post-M5 hardening is specified in\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:13:on the completion audit's confirmation that all five milestones of\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:15:collab/1790871424000-qa-yin-vm-linker-spec-completion-audit.md\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:31:`:yin.link/trees` on by-identity outcomes and `:tree-unavailable`;\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:41:- `docs/design/yin.vm.dependency-completion.md` - the work-item fixed\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:242:>   (`:tree-unavailable` at step 2), distinct from a known tree whose\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:988:(step state budget)             ; -> {:state s :completions [...]\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1030:the worklist needs (a part, under `:parts-fn`), and take completions.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1034:A completion is the step-6 result or a refusal, tagged with its link id:\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1042:A link with no completion yet is `:pending`; the caller steps again\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1055:completion and never reuses the id.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1071:loop until the one link completes, because `step` hands each completion\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1073:completion `fetch` waits for. Liveness is the drive's: a drive whose\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1933:  (`yin.vm.dependency-completion.md`, superseded at phase 8 by\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:2191:document in its status line (2026-09-25); when the completion audit\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:2192:(collab/1790871424000-qa-yin-vm-linker-spec-completion-audit.md)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:2333:          src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc, yin/vm/ffi.cljc, yin/vm/completion.cljc,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:2412: 5. The B6 predecessor's completion criteria hold for all four formats\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md:727:  outstanding id or an undelivered completion, so what an abandon leaves\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md:3400:  `yin.vm.completion` report no `:missing :footprints` for the module.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md:3593:- `(abandon)` during a load ends the require; the load's later completion\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md:3787:completion evidence; an unknown append remains undischarged.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md:3955:state, and recorded successor at completion. Queries derive projections\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md:4043:  authoritative completion records. Completion forms one acyclic\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md:4133:   driver advances a pending wait only on its correlated completion.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md:4138:   answer `:awaiting-completion`; it is not a prerequisite for reporting. An\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md:4139:   accepted report commits the completion identity. A release or policy lapse\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md:4146:   A successor offer is eligible only after that predecessor completion;\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md:4151:   release. Policy-reclaim completion needs no release acknowledgment: finish a\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md:4303:   host matrix, dynamic-reason checks, and refusal cases. Fix any resource,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md:4319:   reclaim epochs, op-id/intent/result records, input replay, and completion\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md:4330:   composition; do not claim full UCF closure from milestone completion.\nOWNER DIRECTIONS RECORDED THIS SESSION (all in memory): (1) foreign-principal modules are NOT auto-refused: trust is a configurable policy, the domain of ShiBi capability tokens, which are only conceptual but have the shape \"everything is a stream, ShiBi is an interpreter of that stream\"; (2) importing modules over a network is part of yin.vm.linker: NO new machinery in the REPL for it (the REPL only configures); (3) the linker is LANGUAGE-BLIND: all languages compile to the universal AST; the VM and linker never know the source language; there is no \"Clojure may use this module, Python may not\"; an admission question concerns principals (keys), addresses (A) and names plus a composition-owned holder context, never a language/frontend/[id revision]; (4) cmd: do not use unless told; kimi-k3 never; glm out except the mob exception; codex back; implementation on claude (opus), reviews on codex; retrospective rule: even mechanical master changes get a different-family review before landing.\nIN FLIGHT at handoff (do not kill; check, they may have finished): (a) opus AD-2 in /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-ad2 (branch admission-ad2, UNCOMMITTED): deletes `principal-admission` and the legacy `:admit` hook, DHT import tests compose `:admission`, renames the foreign-principal test to an-untrusted-principal-is-refused-on-every-vm-test, adds allow and second-publisher head-change cases; brief collab/1792250000000-engineer-ad2.prompt.md, log collab/1792250000000-engineer-ad2.claude-opus-5-5.stdout.log, report to datomworld-ad2/collab/1792250000000-engineer-ad2.findings.md; waits on codex review then ff master. The DHT import artifact must stay unchanged. (b) fable round 2 of the admission-in-linker design: collab/1792262000000-architect-admission-in-linker-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md (brief collab/1792262000000-architect-admission-in-linker-r2.prompt.md); round 1 (collab/1792260000000-architect-admission-in-linker.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md) was REJECTED by codex (collab/1792261000000-reviewer-admission-in-linker.findings.md: false driver-inversion fact, exposure claim, tick-to-VM handoff for a late allow, AL-1 boundary) and then superseded by the language-blind correction (the :yin.link/importer key is deleted).\nNEXT, in order: (1) read the fable round-2 design; send it to codex for re-review (scope contract: block only on in-scope P0/P1); bring design + review to the owner BEFORE dispatching engineers (it moves the link-pair interpreter and admission from yin.repl.* into yin.vm.linker.*, slices AL-0 docs, AL-1 pure namespace relocation, AL-2 REPL reduction + handoff, AL-3 subject/context plumbing, AL-4 trust commands as configuration; the pinned-dependency discharge fix in the engine's link-install with L-d). (2) AD-2: when opus reports, codex review, commit only the AD-2 files on the branch, rebase, ff master from the main checkout, push. (3) HOLD AD-3 (REPL trust commands, session key) until the redesign decides where trust configuration lives. (4) After that: F2 (REPL catalog selection and per-[id revision] session state), the linker pin fix with L-d, I4, then I5-I7/C2 S5/safepoints per the register-VM cutover plan.\nDecisions waiting on the owner: adopt the mob's proposed standing review rule (stop on satisfied gates not a round count; block only on an in-scope P0/P1 or a P2 in claimed acceptance; findings in code the slice should not have written mean revert; known-gaps ledger per track); an independent qwen vote (rerun with collab/ stripped); whether the remote test servers (shiva/jupiter) are cleared (the owner said the test optimization was still being finalized: until told, run everything on the laptop with the new ladder: bb test:sub:clj per iteration, bb test:sub yin.repl yang.python at checkpoints, bb test:changed at landing, --slow only for slow tests touched, the full slow tier at phase boundaries).\nLessons: (a) before `git worktree remove` copy the worktree's untracked collab/ files to main (I lost the I3 engineer reports and the parked linked-REPL tests); (b) `cmd -p` runs: use a non-plan mode, explicit non-interactive instructions, `--output-format json` and check stopReason; permission_denied means a shell call was refused; use --yolo only inside a throwaway worktree copy; (c) the documented `clojure -A:test -M file` runs the whole suite: use `clojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:t {:extra-paths [\"test\"]}}}' -M:t file`; (d) Claude opus runs die at the session limit: briefs must tell the engineer to write the report early; the continuation pattern (untrusted tree, read the predecessor's report) worked each time; (e) estimate review rounds from measured file times (design round 15-25 min, codex review 2-10 min), not guesses; (f) my timing for lane runs: a full yang.python Node+Dart slow sequence is hours on this laptop.\nDelegates this session: fable-5.1 (admission design rounds 1-3, S4/S6-S7 earlier, the linker redesign), codex gpt-6.1-sol (reviews), opus-5-5 (engineers), glm-5.3 and deepseek-v4-pro and qwen3.8-max (mob only).\n\n## 2026-10-14 20:45 +07 — orchestrator log: admission track AD-0 through AL-4 and L-d landed\nCreated-GMT: 2026-10-14 13:45:00 GMT\nCoding-Agent: claude (sonnet-5-5) orchestrator seat\nTree: `master@08a3a722`, pushed\nDone: Landed admission AD-0..AD-2 and AL-0..AL-4 (admission is the linker's: `yin.vm.linker.interpreter`/`admission`, holder context, `reconfigure`; the REPL only configures via `--dht-trust`, `(trust)`, `(untrust)`, `(trusted)`), and L-d (`d0920f2b`, engine `link-install` refuses `:dependency-pin-mismatch` before lifting; fable APPROVE-WITH-NITS, no P0/P1). Slow tier at `355bd84b` found `dht-end-to-end-test` red on all hosts (readers declared but did not trust the publisher; fixed in `08a3a722`). Quick tier at `08a3a722`: JVM 4,209 tests 1 known failure; Node 4,152 green; Dart 4,103 passed 1 known failure.\nOwner directions applied: foreign-principal trust is a configurable ShiBi-style policy; importing over a network is the linker's job, no REPL machinery; the linker is language-blind; implementation to codex (gpt-6.1-sol), fable reviews only; no cmd, glm, kimi-k3; use shiva for lanes.\nLessons: AL-2 tests used `with-redefs` (shiva found Dart compile and 4 Node errors) so spies are JVM-only with `:cljd` first; JVM and Node bb lanes collide in one clone (`build:yin-repl-peer`), use separate clones; slow-tagged tests are invisible to the quick tier, so run the slow tier at phase boundaries; copy worktree `collab/` to main before removing a worktree; the 90-minute review estimate was wrong (measured 2-25 min).\nOpen: `semantic-register.scan-test/scanners-agree-on-the-c4-modules` golden mismatch (JVM, Node; not ours, register-VM seat); known non-ours reds: JVM `rows.cljc` sweep, Dart datagram refusals, Node store-test two-worker (flaky); Dart slow tier has 4 unattributed failures; fable's five AL-4 P3 nits (collab/1792330000000-al4-nits-followup.md); owner decisions pending (Q6 review rule, shiva scratch clones); relocation note collab/1792286000000-orchestrator-note-linker-relocation.md to relay; next slices I4, F2, then I5-I7, C2 S5; DHT large-blob transport (DHT seat); L-e (linker seat).\n\n## 2026-10-14 23:30 +07 — orchestrator seat handoff (I4 next)\nCreated-GMT: 2026-10-14 16:30:00 GMT\nCoding-Agent: claude (sonnet-5-5) orchestrator seat\nTree: `master@28ce8249`, pushed; no tasks running; shiva idle\nDone: Landed L-d (`d0920f2b`), the dht-end-to-end trust fix (`08a3a722`), the AL-4 nits (`28ce8249`, fable APPROVE-WITH-NITS, quick tier only known failures), adopted the Q6 review rule and started `docs/agents/known-gaps.md` (owner 2026-10-14), relayed the linker-relocation note and the scan-test golden mismatch to `yin.vm.semantic-register`. Fable's I4 scoping design is in `collab/1792341000000-architect-i4-scoping.claude-fable-5-1.stdout.log` (try-require as data, registry pin invariant, derived eagerness, five slices L-d-1..L-d-3, I4-a, I4-b).\nDecisions: Owner handed orchestration to another coding agent. Three I4 owner questions are pending (unpinned optional imports; bare primitive vs host module; ModuleNotFoundError scope