post-merge quick tier green.\nPhase 8 (Fable's plan: `collab/1792560000000-architect-phase8-plan.report.md`; slices 8ab, 8c, 8d, 8e, 8f, 8g): 8ab and 8d are implemented by codex and pushed. 8ab: both descriptors lose `:dim/lift-to` and declare `:hash :blake3`; the six surviving hash sites (`debruijn_code`, `debruijn_register_code`, `debruijn`) use `jing/blake3`; 49 distinct constants regenerated and reproducible (`collab/1792620000000-8ab-regen.clj`, byte-identical twice); descriptor diff vs HEAD is exactly the two rows; no A address moved. 8d: 16 old-codec test files (141 deftests), `lift_support`, `v2_support`, `checkpoint_fixtures`, three fixtures and the scalars minter removed; surviving helpers moved to `rows_support`; `handoff.cljc` (3783 lines) and `checkpoint.cljc` are RETAINED until 8f because `test/yang/python/antlr/int_heap_test.cljc:241` (`cell-refusal`, an other-seat C4 file, untouched) still calls `handoff/export-task` and cannot be ported without editing the walker/old-kernel harness; codex also made one trivial port in `test/yang/python/antlr/int_contract_test.cljc` (`an-image-carries-no-profile-test` now uses a semantic-register machine, a fork row pack and `rows/lower-task`): tell the other seat.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
