{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '3328,3375p' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md; sed -n '3392,3406p' docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md; sed -n '232,248p' docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md; sed -n '61,72p' src/cljc/datomworld/demo/continuation_handoff.cljc; sed -n '330,340p' src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/bytecode-vm-optimization.md; head -12 src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows/checkpoint.cljc; rg -n 'partial|noise|live reader|park beside' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md test/yin/vm/semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc; sed -n '1,45p' test/yin/vm/semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"   the epoch is recovered and raised, never reset. Stage: C for the\n   authority facts and their atomic provenance, including through a\n   remote reflection; D for the holder, which answers\n   `:yin.k/not-holder` and releases on an invalid binding.\n8. Admission order and outcomes (7.7.8, 7.9). One fixture per check\n   in order: unreadable authority, wrong author, stale epoch, stale\n   lease, closed occurrence, a foreign id, an inherited id from a\n   closed ancestor, equal intent, different intent, fresh commit.\n   Add a cross-target conflict: one id sent to a second enrolled\n   target answers `:intent-conflict` from the shared namespace and\n   quarantines the occurrence. Add forged outcomes: a `:committed`\n   and an `:intent-conflict` from an unattributed author discharge\n   nothing and quarantine nothing. Add an unknown-effect transport\n   error, cut both before and after the remote commit: the id is\n   retained, the retry goes through the fenced boundary, and it\n   commits once or replays the result already held. Add an\n   unreadable accepted checkpoint: an inherited id answers\n   `:suspended` with tenure, quarantine, and dedup state unchanged,\n   and a stale holder still answers `:stale`. Add a snapshot\n   variant that keeps an id and changes its intent or the root\n   counter: the authority refuses it. Assert the exact\n   outcome map of 7.9 for each and that stale wins over an existing\n   record. Stage: C for the consumer, D for the driver.\n9. Bounds (7.7.8). A counter at 2^52-1 assigns nothing and refuses\n   export. An epoch at 2^52-1 is tested twice: while valid, its\n   grant activates and its effects commit; after the reclaim that\n   would increment it, the lapse is recorded, nothing is granted,\n   no successor is eligible, and admission answers `:suspended`\n   before tenure. The values 2^52 and -1 are refused on the bytes.\n   Stage: C for the epoch, D for the sequence.\n10. **Amended after 7 (2026-10-14)** — Reason: 7d ports Stage E to the canonical kernel and distinguishes host evidence.\n    Composition (linker 14.2.4). Crash, partition, reclaim and completion\n    contracts run through semantic-kernel source/receiver compositions\n    using packs.\n    **Amended after 7 (2026-10-14)** — Reason: the fence is journaled after both durable stores.\n    Recovery format 2 is stored before the whole pack; both are stored durably before the fence is journaled and before any offer.\n    Pack addresses name offers, checkpoints\n    and report results; the baseline includes the structural root.\n    Equal-baseline alternatives retain that root in another row order;\n    an id-counter variant changes root and is `:variant-conflict`.\n    Canonical emit sorts rows, while decode admits unsorted alternatives.\n    The 7d report records local JVM acceptance and a clean JVM/JVM\n    process gate; it does not close Node/Dart or killed four-pair JVM/Node\n    acceptance. Stage: E (7d), pending the orchestrator's host matrix.\n    The REPL custody gap is accepted until phase 8; backend fragment\n    checks (continuation §4.6) remain separate from Stage E.\n\nCanonical fixtures prove grammar parity. They do not prove\n- An undefined export writes nothing.\n- The footprint of 5.2, with no prerequisite outside master: a tree that\n  defines and reads store keys answers exactly `ast-requirements`'\n  `:store-keys`; an effectful declared primitive and a stream tag each add\n  their effects; a required manifest adds its footprint's effects and none\n  of its store keys; a missing required manifest, an unprofiled primitive,\n  an FFI call and a parked id each refuse with their reason and write\n  nothing. The manifest it produces makes\n  `yin.vm.completion` report no `:missing :footprints` for the module.\n- `yin.vm.linker/local-runtime` exists and the linker tests' runtime delegates\n  to it; no behaviour changes. `yin.repl.link` adopts it in L3.\n\n**L1 -- the staged load, the backlog, the publication result.** Files:\n`src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc`,\n`src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc` (reason and result rendering only),\n>   address is A itself, and the canonical vector stays obtainable\n>   independently of any native-image entry, and so does a tree it was\n>   projected from: the composition's `source-index` maps A to the set\n>   of tree addresses it knows (populated at publication and from every\n>   verified manifest), and a by-identity outcome for any format carries\n>   that set as `:yin.link/trees`. A is not a key to one tree (several\n>   ASTs project to one A); the unitarity invariant of `datom.world.md`\n>   (the AST is retrievable wherever code is lowered) is satisfied when\n>   at least one member is known. A native image for which the serving\n>   composition knows no tree is a composition defect\n>   (`:tree-unavailable` at step 2), distinct from a known tree whose\n>   read fails, which is the medium's ordinary `:absent`\n>   (`yin.vm.semantic.derivations.md` §9.2, 2026-10-11). The\n>   derivation record of\n>   §8.1 for format `f` leads from the canonical tree to A and from A to\n>   the native image, recording the checksum as evidence, not identity.\n> - **The AST walker** (`:yin.ast/code`, §5.1): the tree's root row\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Semantic VM: the continuation is the datoms that travel\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; A semantic VM between instructions is a code segment plus register window —\n;; {:segment :pc :value :window :env :k} — all plain data (yin.vm.semantic.md\n;; §7). Nothing travels off-stream: the handoff batch is the AST's\n;; `:yin/*` datoms followed by one registers datom whose value is EDN\n;; text, so the receiver rebuilds the machine from bytes it read, not from a\n;; host object it shares with the sender. Definitions the program made\n;; (symbol-keyed store entries) travel with the registers; primitives,\n- Current: `bytecode-vm-optimization` (`d4b16c1`)\n- Baseline: `master` (`d66b250`)\n\nNotes for reproducibility:\n\n- In the temporary `master` worktree, a compile-only compatibility patch was\n  applied to `vm/opcase` macro expansion so CLJD could compile. Runtime\n  workload and benchmark parameters were kept identical.\n\nRun results (`mean_total_ms`):\n\n(ns yin.vm.ucf.rows.checkpoint\n  \"The rows inspector of phase 7a (phase-7 plan §3.3): the custody grammar\n   of a version-3 row pack, checked on its canonical bytes, and the\n   operation baseline it carries. It replaces yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint at the\n   authority's three call sites (grant/offer!, completion/report!,\n   admission's accepted-baseline); the version-1/2 inspector stays for the\n   old codec's tests until phase 8.\n\n   A pack has two identities. The **pack address** is the BLAKE3 segment\n   address of the pack's canonical bytes: the storage key, the one a\n   dao.jing content store verifies on put, and the ledger's :yin.k/id. The\n   **root id** is the :task row's own content address inside the pack: the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:925:and stream-id response-stream. A partial carried pair is rejected; the\n(ns yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test\n  \"Phase 6b: the safepoint harness on the :semantic lane\n   (docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md §5, §8.2).\n\n   Each row of the §5.2 matrix is built twice under each of the four\n   segment wrappers: the reference build is satisfied and run on its own\n   machine; the handoff build is lifted with rows/lift-task, lowered with\n   rows/lower-task into a fresh receiver over the toy channel, relifted at\n   once, then satisfied through the source's streams. Result and effect\n   trace equal the reference (law 1); the relift equals the lift by root\n   id under rows/canonical-under (law 2); the pending's reason is the\n   observed wait's (law 3); every lifted frame passes the validator\n   (law 6). Row 20 runs once, outside the wrappers.\n\n   Phase 6c adds the two de Bruijn lanes (§5.3): a world built under\n   *lane* :stack or :register runs A's derived image on that kernel and\n   lifts and lowers through yin.vm.semantic.layout. Law 4 (one\n   root id on all three lanes under canonical-under), law 5 (six ordered\n   lowering pairs, each continuing to the reference result) and the\n   layout refusals close the file.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n            [yin.vm.ledger :as ledger]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as sr]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n            [yin.vm.parity-test :as b0]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.analysis :as analysis]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.corpus :as corpus]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.frame :as frame]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.frame-test :as ft]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.layout :as layout]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as s]))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc'\ns=open(p).read(); s+='''\n\n(deftest collection-row-keys-use-content-equality\n  ;; CLJS Numbers erase integral float kind and zero sign; explicit float64\n  ;; values keep both distinctions present on every host.\n  (doseq [keys [[(cbor/float64 0.0) (cbor/float64 -0.0)]\n               [1 (cbor/float64 1.0)]]\n          kind [:map :set]]\n    (let [body (cursor-cell-body :s 0)\n          slots (if (= kind :set)\n                  (conj (mapv #(vector :lit %) keys) [:cursor-cell :x])\n                  (vec (mapcat #(vector [:lit %] [:cursor-cell :x]) keys)))\n          task (assoc-in (task-node [[:x body]] [:row (rows/node kind slots)])\n                         [:slots 5] (rows/node :bindings ['anchor [:cursor-cell :x]]))\n          wire (rows/emit task)\n          refusal (error #(rows/decode wire))]\n      (is (not (apply cbor/content= keys)))\n      (is (nil? refusal) (pr-str refusal))\n      (when-not refusal\n        (is (= (:yin.k/root wire) (:yin.k/root (rows/emit (rows/decode wire)))))))))\n''';open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nclojure -M:test -e :slow -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-test > /tmp/followup-rows-red.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
