e's entries). Findings: muse merged slice 8d into srvm-phase8 (4b5752a3) with Node and Dart red (`yin.vm.ucf.rows-test/numeric-scalars-round-trip-through-rows`: a literal AST slot rejects JS/Dart BigInt carriers; the lanes had finished and were unread); fixed by codex as `srvm-phase8d-fix@9b4b250a` (test-only; Node 87 tests/0 errors, Dart +65, JVM 99 green), merged as 4ec2c198 on lane evidence plus a mutant, review by a different family dispatched retroactively. 8ab rebased by muse onto master 72592bd9 as 2b9f2b47 plus pins commit d3530037, pushed as srvm-phase8ab-r2 (never force-push the old branch); Node 323 tests/0 failures, Dart +262, jupiter quick 13/13. (2) CORRECTION of units that were never logged by this seat (the log's rule is one entry per coherent unit; only handoff entries were written): phases 5b/5c (merged e5df547a), BLAKE3 seals and profile digest (4529b5bd), free-environment retention seam (e0b0006f), BLAKE3 for the DHT cookie/CBOR fixtures/ANTLR manifest (cbdf983f), slice 6a with discovery-order cursor cell numbering (73af17ac), 6b (1db08f7d), 6c (781a9ba8), docs amendments (e2886a6f, 7a40502c), phase 7 slices 7a-7e landed on master as 67b98907 via the integration branch srvm-phase7, merged-branch repairs (lint, scan golden). Their evidence is in the commits and in the collab/ reports/findings named in each slice; each was gated by a non-author review and the three-host lanes unless stated below.\n11261:Decisions: Deviations from orchestrator.md/team.md by this seat, recorded so they are visible: (a) commits to slice branches before the independent review (to let shiva/jupiter lanes run on pushed commits); nothing reached master without review, lanes and green gates; (b) merged and deleted merged worktrees/branches (26 worktrees after `cp -n` of their collab/) on the standing authority recorded in memory, not on an explicit instruction for each; (c) the orchestrator made design-leaning calls itself where an Architect or the owner should have: the row-algorithm refusal status (`:yin.k/undecodable :row-algorithm` chosen over `:profile-mismatch` to match the transport spec) and algorithm-aware verification of carried addresses, the 7a D1 landing strategy (integration branch srvm-phase7, master only at the end) and D2 (root inside the baseline): escalated for Architect confirmation after the fact (collab/1792670000000-architect-f1-confirm.prompt.md); the 6c Q2 'rejected' inference (owner confirmed 'its fine the way it is'); (d) 7b was partly authored by opus (retained partial edit) and reviewed by Fable (same Claude family): reviewer independence was not met for that partial edit; (e) briefs and reports written before today lack the artifact header (Session-ID, Implementers) and several delegate runs were not captured as tasks: from now on each dispatch carries the full header and a task; (f) team.md's cost table reserves codex for architectural review; the owner's rulings of 2026-10-11 and 2026-10-13 route implementation to codex ('route implementation to codex models'), and 2026-10-15 adds glm and cmd: routing-status.md has not been updated and needs an owner-relayed entry. Unattended-run rules the seat set for itself: collab/1792660000000-orchestrator-handoff-unattended.md.\n\nFAIL in (collection-row-keys-use-content-equality) (rows_test.cljc:1333)\n#:yin.k{:status :yin.k/undecodable, :kind :duplicate-key, :path [:segment/blake3-b8dfa3959b90f57c0bf83b85e59518187bb88aa88ae6156f34626bcff27f46d0]}\nexpected: (nil? refusal)\n  actual: (not (nil? #:yin.k{:status :yin.k/undecodable, :kind :duplicate-key, :path [:segment/blake3-b8dfa3959b90f57c0bf83b85e59518187bb88aa88ae6156f34626bcff27f46d0]}))\n{:test 3, :pass 23, :fail 2, :error 0}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
