{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^### 3|''^## 3|''^## 10|''^###.*8'\"' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md; sed -n '280,295p' test/yin/vm/semantic/linearize_test.cljc; head -11 src/cljd/yin/register_bench_cljd.cljd; head -9 test/bench/yin_vm_bench.cljc; sed -n '1,10p' src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/jfr_benchmark_analysis.md; sed -n '266,274p' src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/jfr_benchmark_analysis.md; tail -15 /tmp/followup-quick.log\"","aggregated_output":"387:## 3. The canonical grammar\n389:### 3.1 Expression-structured by construction\n491:### 3.2 Exclusive definitions by structured paths\n506:### 3.3 The lowering walk and the minting order\n579:### 3.4 Well-formedness\n847:### 8.1 Static facts per pc: def, use, live\n876:### 8.2 A → R: the de Bruijn register image\n971:### 8.3 A → H: the de Bruijn stack image\n989:### 8.4 Verification\n1056:## 10. Migration\n                    {:source :medium}]]\n      (is (= :origin (:rule (throws-ex-data #(linearize/project-rows bc origin))))\n          (pr-str origin)))))\n\n\n(def ^:private projection-worked-example\n  \"`((fn [x] (+ x 1)) 10)`, yin.vm.semantic.md §3.1 (canonical projection).\"\n  (app (lam '[x] (tail (app (v '+) (v 'x) (lit 1)))) (lit 10)))\n\n\n(def ^:private projection-corpus\n  {:projection-worked-example projection-worked-example,\n   :literal (lit 42),\n   :nil-literal (lit nil),\n   :zero-arity-call (app (lam [] (lit 1))),\n   :nested-lambdas (app (app (lam '[a] (tail (lam '[b] (tail (app (v '+) (v 'a) (v 'b))))))\n(ns yin.register-bench-cljd\n  \"Benchmark the Yin VM v2 evaluators on Dart.\n\n   `yin.register-bench-cljd` drove the v1 register VM. This benchmark drives\n   `yin.vm.ast-walker` and the linear `yin.vm.semantic` VM\n   (`docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md#history`, retired v3 benchmark) on one workload, and its numbers\n   are not comparable with the v1 register numbers. The workload and the\n   sampling discipline are carried over unchanged so the runs answer the\n   same question about their own engine.\n\n   The timed region is `vm/run` alone. VM construction, the lowering, and the\n(ns bench.yin-vm-bench\n  \"Semantic VM Phase 4: the ast-walker against the linear semantic VM on\n   `yin.vm` (`docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md#history`, retired v3 benchmark).\n\n   The workload is the historic tail-recursive countdown from the deleted\n   `yin.vm.bytecode-bench`, so the ratios read against the 1.32x walker and\n   1.0–1.1x register/stack line in `docs/cesk-space-optimization.md`.\n\n   The timed region is `vm/run` alone. VM construction, AST → datoms, the\n# Why the v2 Semantic VM is 7.19× faster than the v1 Semantic VM\n\nRole: VM Architect · Model: glm-5.3 · 2026-09-14\nInputs: `profiles/v1.jfr`, `profiles/v2.jfr` (JDK 21.0.2, `settings=profile`,\ndump-on-exit), `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md#history` (retired v3 kernel), `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc`,\nv1 sources read from `master` (`git show master:src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc` etc.).\n\nHeadline under analysis: v1 semantic 15.158 ms/run vs v2 semantic 2.108 ms/run\n(n=1000 tail-recursive countdown), ratio **7.19×**.\n\n7.19×. The interpreter-only 3.2× is the like-for-like architectural number;\nit is also consistent with the walker-relative measurements in\n`docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md#history` (retired v3 benchmark) (semantic 0.115× of walker on the JVM,\nwhere the walker itself is the surviving record-per-step machine).\n\n## 7. Why each architectural difference is worth what it is (code → JFR)\n\n1. **Registers in `loop` locals, record touched only at exits**\n   (`vm-hot`, `put-registers`). Deletes v1's 1.47 GB of `SemanticVM` copies\nTesting datomworld.demo.continuation-handoff-test\n\nTesting datomworld.demo.earth-moon-scene-test\n\nTesting datomworld.demo.solar-system-scene-test\n\nTesting datomworld.demo.voxel-controls-test\n\nTesting datomworld.demo.voxel-input-test\n\nTesting datomworld.demo.voxel-runner-test\n\nTesting datomworld.demo.voxel-scene-test\n\nTesting yang.clojure.stream-eval-test\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
